        ['Explain three differences between an informal letter and a formal letter.', ['Addresses', 'Salutation/heading', 'Tone', 'Closing'], 'An informal letter has one address (the writer\'s); a formal letter has two. An informal letter uses a friendly salutation such as "Dear Esi"; a formal letter uses "Dear Sir/Madam" and a heading. An informal letter closes with "Your friend"; a formal letter closes with "Yours faithfully/sincerely" and the full name.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 3, 'theory', 6],
        ['Write a letter to your grandmother thanking her for a gift she sent you.', ['Layout', 'Salutation', 'Thanks and details', 'News', 'Close'], 'Address and date; "Dear Grandma,"; greetings and hope she is well; thank her for the gift and describe how you are using it; share family or school news; promise to visit; close "Your loving grandchild," and name.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 3, 'theory', 10],
        ['Write a letter to your cousin abroad telling him about a festival in your town.', ['Layout', 'Salutation', 'Description of festival', 'Personal feelings', 'Close'], 'Address and date; "Dear Kwaku,"; greetings; describe the festival (name, when it is held, activities such as drumming, durbar and food); say how you felt; invite him to come next year; close "Your cousin," and name.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 3, 'theory', 10],
